WEBVTT

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:01.820
Thank you.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.680
Looks like a good one coming on.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.920
Yes, I'm afraid. The old one in particular.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.520
You ask me, it's going to be black.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:29.980
Long time since we had one of them.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:31.620
Well, good night. Good night.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.420
What are we stopping for?

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.230
The rest of the night, I should think, Governor.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:08.090
What street is this?

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.160
It was Spark Lane when I seen it last.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:11.520
Anything I can do?

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:12.680
I want to get to Dorset Square.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:13.560
Not tonight, sir.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.790
Your best bet is the Royal Parks Hotel.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:16.600
Where's that?

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:17.600
Just here, sir.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:18.320
Follow me.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.650
Bring the bags, will you?

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:22.990
Yes, sir.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.420
Careful, please step here, sir.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.170
All right, thanks very much.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:32.940
Thanks, Governor.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:33.600
We'll go up there.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:34.610
All right.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:42.260
Come on bar, please, just for the night.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.100
I'm sorry, sir.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.880
The best I can offer you is the small suite.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.460
We're almost full owing to the park.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:47.640
Park, all right.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:48.750
317.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:49.410
This way, sir.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.130
Mesa's all right, but Mesa's nice.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:48.610
Don't be so unpatriotic, Michael.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.540
Fog is one of our greatest attractions.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.420
That's what the Americans come to see us for.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.520
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.160
the committee wished me to announce

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:59.520
that owing to the extremely bad fog tonight...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.400
Those of you who have any considerable distance to travel

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.880
are advised to stop overnight in the hotel.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.450
Now, now. May I take you home, Leslie?

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:09.870
No, thank you, Michael.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.500
I think I'll take the committee's advice and try and stay here tonight.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:14.540
I doubt if you'll get a room.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:18.110
Look at the crowd storming the reception plant there.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:23.580
Just do leave it to me.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:24.590
Good night, Michael.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:38.560
I'm sorry, but it's not a single room we have.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.380
We have enough room. That was the last room.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:45.800
I will ask the manager. Monsieur Bianco, he can do something for you.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.040
We will, I'm sure. Monsieur Bianco, please.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:52.640
Please, please, please.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:56.150
Ladies and gentlemen, every room in this hotel is taken.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:59.980
The best I can do for you is to offer your accommodation in the lounge and in the restaurant.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:03.940
There are some very comfortable divans and chairs, and you will be welcome.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:13.260
Some of the guests with sweets will be willing to give up their sitting rooms for one night.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.650
Oh, perhaps. I will try.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.890
Will you come with me, madam? This way, please.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:34.630
with breakfast. China tea, two boiled eggs, medium done, the time from October.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:35.930
Thank you very much, sir. Good night, sir.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.920
You good? We'll ring me when you get them, will you?

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:50.380
Just a moment, lady. Perhaps the gentleman in this sea will help.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.370
I am the manager of this hotel.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:03.200
How do you know?

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:08.460
On to the fog, many of the guests who have been attending a bowl find it impossible to get home.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:14.630
I am most anxious to find bedrooms for the ladies, and I hope you could help me.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:15.880
In what way?

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:22.330
Well, we have several divans in the lounge, still vacant, and the chairs on the ground floor are very comfortable.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.230
You want me to give up this suite, don't you?

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:25.150
If you would, please.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:28.340
I see. Now, let me make myself clear.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:29.980
I've been traveling for two...

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:34.250
I've had an extremely filthy crossing. My train was two hours late at Victorian Station.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:38.320
I'm very tired and very cross. In fact, quite wild with fatigue.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.460
But I am the legal possessor of this suite,

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.540
and I'm determined to defend it with every power in my possession.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:44.590
Good night.

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:51.360
Sir, if you would just give up your sitting room, I could accommodate four ladies.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:56.040
No. No. No, I know the ladies and I know myself.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.300
They'd have me out of here in five minutes.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:59.960
I'm very sorry. What I did really, very badly is a good...

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:04.500
And I shall have that, though every lady in London thinks me a cad, a brute and a beast.

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:05.000
Good night.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:11.440
By the way, is there a do not disturb card there?

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:14.110
Very, dear.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:16.880
You might hang it on the door for me as you go out, will you?

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:20.230
Very well.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:59.310
I'm sorry, dear, it really wasn't my fault. I really am terribly disappointed, really.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.500
I'm quite, quite heartbroken, dear.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:03.460
Why?

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.560
Well, dear, the train was late.

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:06.870
Late?

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:09.240
Yes, there was a fog.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:10.770
A F-O-G.

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:13.470
F as in falch, dear.

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:15.590
No, dear.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.680
F-O as in osteopath.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:20.760
What?

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:23.500
Why don't you spend it with your husband for a change?

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:26.260
No, no, no, no, Dad.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:27.500
Go on, go to sleep.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:28.850
Can't you read?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.660
No, did I. I wasn't talking to you. I'm very sorry, darling.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.080
Well, some of it's... this will tell you.

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:36.200
Well, I'll read it for you. It says, do not disturb.

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:37.760
Aren't you?

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:39.060
No, I still don't.

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:41.870
Oh, go on, darling. He's never ever looking at anybody else.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:43.230
Oh, silly.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.240
No, it does not. It's more polite.

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:50.880
It says, please do not disturb.

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:11.900
Well? Well, what?

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:14.030
That's just what I'd like to know.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:17.140
To whom do I owe the unexpected pleasure to first visit?

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:18.280
I mean, what's the general idea?

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:20.260
I was just looking for something.

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:25.570
Well, whatever it is, I'm afraid you won't find it in my room.

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:29.670
I'm very tired. I was looking for a place to sleep.

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:31.980
Oh.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.000
And this seems practically ideal for that purpose.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:38.220
Yes, that's just what I was thinking when you came bursting in.

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:39.890
I didn't burst. I crept.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.760
Oh, may I ask when you propose to creep out again?

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:45.480
Oh, after the usual eight hours and breakfast.

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:48.790
Oh, really? So we're going to bunk in together, are we?

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.640
There are two rooms, one for each of us.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:54.520
Yes, but both beds are in here.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:56.510
There's a couch in there.

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:57.970
You can have the couch.

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:06.600
With all the shameless impudence, was there ever anything more female

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.220
and you actually thought you could get away with it?

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.590
If you had any decent feelings, you'd insist on turning out.

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:13.590
Did you or did you not hear what I said to the manager?

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:16.150
Naturally, I overheard some of it.

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:19.360
So little feeling that you would touch my bed from under my very nose,

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:20.960
knowing perfectly well that I've been up for two nights

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:22.000
and I've got a hard day's work tomorrow,

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.720
assuming I can't resist your fascination.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:28.620
I'm really very sleepy. Will you please go?

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:35.340
You don't really mean that. You're much too nice to turn me out.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:36.920
Nice?

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:40.670
Yeah, young lady, you don't know me. The trouble with me is that I'm weak.

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:43.830
A charming young girl like you could put anything over on me in five minutes.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.310
But at least I know my weakness, so I force myself to be rude.

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:48.190
Sometimes even brutal.

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.440
You do like talking about yourself, don't you?

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:52.160
Well, yes, most men do.

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:54.960
But at least they know the truth about themselves. Women don't.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:56.800
They only know the truth about each other.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.970
Well, we'll have a nice long talk about you some other time.

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:03.380
Now, as you're so very tired, I won't keep you up.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:04.750
So, good night.

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:09.710
What did you say?

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:11.690
I said, good night.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:14.030
Well, yes, I heard you say good night.

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:15.170
But what do you mean by saying good night?

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.510
You can't come here and say things like...

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:18.050
Look here, I'm very, very tired.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:18.610
Would you please go?

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:19.810
You don't mean that.

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:20.610
Oh, yes, I do.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:22.720
I've met too many women like you before.

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:25.280
Conceited, sure of yourself, and sure of your power over men.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.770
Utterly unscrupulous, ruthless, conceited, spoiled.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:29.230
Don't do that.

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:33.910
Yes.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:40.100
Yes, yes, I'm a poor wretched husband waiting for you, sitting at home,

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:43.390
wondering where you are, hoping against hope that his worst fears aren't justified.

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:44.910
And this time, for once, they aren't.

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:47.650
This time, you're with a man who isn't in the least bit stirred by your charms.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:48.790
Now, I must repeat, will you, please?

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:51.590
How do you know so much about women?

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:55.590
Because in my profession, I have to be able to see what's behind those lovely deceiving lips.

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:56.500
Are you a dentist?

00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:56.940
No!

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:02.910
we meet will probably be in court when your husband is suing you for a divorce.

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:05.080
Divorce? Oh, no. He'd never do that.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:06.420
You must have a very beautiful nature.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.400
You've had a very tiring journey, haven't you?

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:09.440
Yes, I have.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:12.420
And it's such a pity that the fog made you late and spoiled your evening.

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:17.260
But remember, it's that same fog that's now keeping me from going home to my dear husband.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:22.390
You don't mind my asking. What is your name?

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:26.050
I do mind a little.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:29.880
Good. You have some sense of discretion anyway. And you may have my couch.

00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:33.950
Come away from you, I might change my mind.

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:43.210
Change.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:53.510
You are a kind, generous, beautiful man.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:28.700
There's a nice thick rug on the floor. Try that.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:29.970
But there are two...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:37.680
Two beds in your room. I'd never dream of such a thing.

00:14:43.350 --> 00:14:45.310
We could move one of the beds in here, couldn't we?

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:51.530
Well, yes, I suppose we could. I'll ring for the waiter.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:54.320
Do you think we should disturb them?

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:58.820
No, no, Prince, we shouldn't.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:01.610
If you'll wait here, I'll bring it in myself.

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:04.060
Come and help you.

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:05.890
I'm ready to help you.

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:08.490
Oh, I wouldn't dream of letting you do it by yourself.

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:10.030
You were kind enough to offer me of it.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:10.910
I must offer you my help.

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:11.670
All right, we'll take that, Emily.

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:13.390
Now, when I say, to me, from you.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:13.990
To me, from you.

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:14.490
No, no, no.

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:15.330
From you, to me.

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:15.950
To me.

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:18.280
From, to me.

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:21.290
I'd better leave this to me.

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:21.750
Hello, ma'am.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:38.580
Get in the house.

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:50.110
So don't wait.

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:12.630
Would anyone ask about a better place to spend the night?

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:13.370
No.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:14.400
Good night.

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:31.320
Thank you.

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:01.780
What is it?

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:06.000
Possibly steep in this costume.

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:07.020
You better take it off.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:11.220
What shall I put on?

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:12.610
As I'm concerned, nothing.

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:15.040
You always think of yourself.

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:20.220
Pajamas?

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:21.580
Take those off the bed.

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:24.510
What's the matter?

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:29.970
Can a man wear a wig and robe with dignity in an English court if this represents his tail?

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.460
Do you think I'll have time to go and buy pajamas?

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:32.560
Then break with her.

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:33.020
With whom?

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:36.960
She who buys pajamas such as these cannot be a good woman.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:38.440
Break with her.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:39.820
We parted six months ago.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:41.450
Then there's some hope for you.

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:43.640
Perhaps...

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:31.760
I wish I could. What do you want?

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:33.800
The elementary right of a wash.

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:35.320
Well, here is the bathroom.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:37.700
But I have to cross your bedroom.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:39.480
Well, you're wearing my pajamas, aren't you?

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:40.620
That's the trouble.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.280
Well, what do you expect me to do? Jump out of the window?

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:45.870
Either that or turn your face to the wall.

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:51.750
I'm facing the wall.

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:56.850
Why don't you move?

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:58.940
Until I tell you.

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:03.070
I shall become giddy if I go on staring at this wallpaper.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:09.060
And the alarm if you're approaching again.

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:45.670
Is that the alarm? What are you doing?

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:59.840
I'm in bed. Didn't you say it once?

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:01.240
Sleep just as well out there.

00:20:01.610 --> 00:20:01.990
It is.

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:03.490
Have it, then.

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.100
It's better for both of us.

00:20:05.590 --> 00:20:06.170
For both of us.

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:09.030
Well, can't you see what a delicate,

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:10.770
what a painful situation I'm in?

00:20:11.260 --> 00:20:12.400
Out there, I'm a guest,

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:13.990
trespassing on a man's chivalry.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.100
And here, with everything around me,

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:18.520
the, uh, that, that.

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:20.870
I feel less like an intruder

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:22.770
and more like the legal owner of the suite.

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:24.160
I see.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:25.950
Your conscience at rest.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:27.920
Think how much better you'd sleep.

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:28.890
All right.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:30.460
You win.

00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:31.460
Oh, no, no, no.

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:33.560
You win over yourself.

00:20:34.020 --> 00:20:34.560
You win.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:41.410
I'll see you one day in the divorce court.

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:43.290
You'll never see me in the divorce court.

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:44.430
Don't you purge yourself!

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:46.280
I shall see you in the divorce court

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:47.740
if this is a sample of your ordinary behavior.

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:49.890
But is there anything wrong in what we do?

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:56.180
Is there anything wrong in what I do?

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:07.500
No. Good night.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:10.140
Good night. Sleep well.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:30.280
Oh

00:22:01.070 --> 00:22:09.430
My book. Give me that book.

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:11.110
You can take any other book but this.

00:22:11.130 --> 00:22:12.130
There is no other book but that.

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:14.040
I simply couldn't give this up.

00:22:14.320 --> 00:22:16.820
I must know who killed the wealthy and wise Chinese banker.

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:17.560
Don't tell me.

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:19.860
I want to do it myself. I've only read half of it.

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:20.860
Here, I'll make you an offer.

00:22:21.720 --> 00:22:23.920
But you can't read the whole book tonight.

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:25.430
Oh, but I very seldom do that.

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:27.090
I read the beginning and I read the end.

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:33.240
Who killed someone so many years?

00:22:33.640 --> 00:22:35.800
Can it have been the mysterious lady in pajamas?

00:24:06.010 --> 00:24:09.740
Good morning, sir. Eight o'clock, sir. Nice morning.

00:24:10.780 --> 00:24:11.840
Your breakfast is served, sir.

00:24:12.580 --> 00:24:12.700
What?

00:24:13.980 --> 00:24:15.730
Your breakfast is served, madam.

00:24:16.310 --> 00:24:17.660
Oh, thank you.

00:24:19.160 --> 00:24:20.740
Would you... would you bring another one, please?

00:24:21.550 --> 00:24:22.730
Another... what, madam?

00:24:24.110 --> 00:24:25.390
Another... another breakfast.

00:24:25.930 --> 00:24:27.460
Certainly, sir. Madam.

00:25:49.950 --> 00:25:52.290
I've had a rotten night's sleep and I've got to be in court by half past ten.

00:25:54.280 --> 00:25:55.320
Yes, we all know what that means.

00:26:00.700 --> 00:26:04.120
Hello. What about my breakfast?

00:26:05.530 --> 00:26:07.770
What? What do you mean I've had two already?

00:26:11.310 --> 00:26:16.050
Second breakfast, madam. I mean, sir.

00:26:16.270 --> 00:26:17.380
What's the matter with you?

00:26:18.090 --> 00:26:22.650
Well, the fog was pretty severe last night, sir,

00:26:22.870 --> 00:26:25.400
and things seemed to be a little disorganized this morning.

00:26:26.110 --> 00:26:27.690
You're telling me? Take that into the other room.

00:26:28.500 --> 00:26:29.970
Yes, sir. What about...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:30.560
That one, sir.

00:26:31.020 --> 00:26:31.760
Better than that, too.

00:26:40.700 --> 00:26:40.920
Morning.

00:26:51.650 --> 00:26:51.750
Hello.

00:26:53.720 --> 00:26:54.100
6347.

00:26:56.800 --> 00:26:57.040
Hello.

00:26:58.330 --> 00:26:59.970
Is his lordship down yet?

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:01.780
No, no, don't disturb him, but, um,

00:27:01.960 --> 00:27:03.960
will you tell him I spent the night at the Royal Parks Hotel?

00:27:04.280 --> 00:27:05.280
Then I'll be along later.

00:27:06.030 --> 00:27:07.590
Well, you know what his lordship's like, Miss Leslie.

00:27:08.100 --> 00:27:10.380
Like he's not even on your tail for being on the towers last night.

00:27:11.160 --> 00:27:13.040
You'd better give me your room number, if you please.

00:27:13.760 --> 00:27:19.080
Oh, beautiful. 317.

00:27:19.580 --> 00:27:21.600
I was talking to the waiter. What did you say?

00:27:22.310 --> 00:27:24.400
317. 317.

00:27:31.440 --> 00:27:33.930
Do you think of everything?

00:27:34.400 --> 00:27:35.460
Breakfast is served, sir.

00:27:36.210 --> 00:27:38.130
Meh. It's ready.

00:27:39.790 --> 00:27:40.370
Good way.

00:27:42.700 --> 00:27:44.020
What is your name?

00:27:44.180 --> 00:27:44.540
Logan.

00:27:45.830 --> 00:27:46.130
Logan.

00:27:46.550 --> 00:27:48.130
No, not Logan. It's not Chinese. Logan.

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:49.540
Don't like it.

00:28:04.440 --> 00:28:04.700
May I?

00:28:04.840 --> 00:28:05.810
Oh, yes, do.

00:28:07.760 --> 00:28:09.060
Only don't mess about.

00:28:16.020 --> 00:28:18.000
You've got to be butter and marmalade.

00:28:30.890 --> 00:28:38.770
Who are these eggs, medium boys?

00:28:39.960 --> 00:28:41.560
Graceful. In a big hotel like this?

00:28:42.090 --> 00:28:42.590
Yours the same?

00:28:43.400 --> 00:28:44.220
Oh, mine are just right.

00:28:55.990 --> 00:28:56.310
Marmalade.

00:28:56.730 --> 00:28:57.890
Probably taste the printed ink.

00:28:59.260 --> 00:28:59.680
No, thank you.

00:29:00.060 --> 00:29:03.180
You must eat something, you know, with a long, hard day's work ahead of you.

00:29:03.300 --> 00:29:04.620
I really don't want to think things.

00:29:07.710 --> 00:29:09.870
Do you mind telling me this morning what your name is?

00:29:11.190 --> 00:29:11.470
Leslie.

00:29:11.630 --> 00:29:14.160
What, Leslie?

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:17.880
What do you mean, what, Les? Lesley's my Christian name.

00:29:18.640 --> 00:29:20.730
Oh, Lesley.

00:29:24.440 --> 00:29:24.940
What's yours?

00:29:30.870 --> 00:29:37.580
You don't like that either?

00:29:39.090 --> 00:29:39.990
Never get used to that.

00:29:40.190 --> 00:29:41.030
Well, who's asking you to?

00:29:41.230 --> 00:29:42.390
Is there anything else you'd like to know?

00:29:42.550 --> 00:29:43.470
Yes, one more thing.

00:29:43.570 --> 00:29:44.650
You always like this in the morning?

00:29:45.120 --> 00:29:46.340
until I had my first cigarette.

00:30:03.612 --> 00:30:05.612
You're very sorry for the woman you're going to marry.

00:30:05.612 --> 00:30:06.912
I shan't marry.

00:30:07.772 --> 00:30:09.372
Unless I can arrange that little divorce for you.

00:30:09.724 --> 00:30:10.564
Hmm.

00:30:10.620 --> 00:30:10.860
Heaven.

00:30:11.196 --> 00:30:11.436
time.

00:30:23.036 --> 00:30:23.536
Thank you very much.

00:30:24.412 --> 00:30:26.732
I told you, I sure don't need your professional services.

00:30:27.260 --> 00:30:28.260
Thanks very much.

00:30:28.348 --> 00:30:29.848
You poor benighted husband, mate.

00:30:30.320 --> 00:30:31.240
Why poor Benitez?

00:30:31.400 --> 00:30:32.220
Because you deceive him.

00:30:32.460 --> 00:30:34.010
I certainly do not.

00:30:34.430 --> 00:30:37.980
Oh, didn't I hear you telephone that you were talking to a waiter?

00:30:38.180 --> 00:30:40.400
I ask you, me, a waiter.

00:30:41.150 --> 00:30:43.330
What did you say you were? A solicitor?

00:30:44.060 --> 00:30:44.540
Solicitor.

00:30:45.060 --> 00:30:46.060
Lawyer, barrister.

00:30:46.200 --> 00:30:49.530
And being a barrister, one does at least learn to judge human character.

00:30:50.360 --> 00:30:52.320
What'll I like that from you in the witness box?

00:30:52.520 --> 00:30:53.940
I know what to think about you, all right?

00:30:54.650 --> 00:30:56.510
That seals my fate with you then, hm?

00:31:00.350 --> 00:31:01.370
You're one price possessor.

00:31:01.470 --> 00:31:03.620
I'm dying to hear it.

00:31:03.720 --> 00:31:06.840
You're a perfect angel in the morning.

00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:08.500
And perfectly inseparable.

00:31:09.720 --> 00:31:10.960
That's the very quality of a woman.

00:31:11.040 --> 00:31:14.620
The wife must be adorable.

00:31:15.380 --> 00:31:18.000
That's a very rash statement, seeing we're complete strangers.

00:31:18.260 --> 00:31:18.920
But anything but.

00:31:19.120 --> 00:31:22.470
We know each other better than most people after they've been married for years.

00:31:22.790 --> 00:31:25.550
We're tied together by invisible bonds.

00:31:25.770 --> 00:31:29.780
How can we partner forever? How can we meet again?

00:31:30.620 --> 00:31:34.310
How can I say the things to you the perfect strangers say to each other?

00:31:35.810 --> 00:31:38.720
I must see you again. Where can they meet?

00:31:39.810 --> 00:31:43.910
Savoy, Embassy, Claritin? Lunch, dinner, supper?

00:31:45.260 --> 00:31:47.320
Today, tomorrow? Tonight?

00:32:00.960 --> 00:32:02.580
Dean, are you or aren't you?

00:32:22.780 --> 00:32:27.220
My dear, it was the creature that lay gloating in bed all night

00:32:27.220 --> 00:32:29.760
while we were rolling about on the billiard table.

00:32:30.190 --> 00:32:30.390
Peace.

00:33:13.340 --> 00:33:29.080
the trays, madam. Very good, sir. I suppose you'd describe this liquid as a concoction of coffee bean. I'll tell you what it is.

00:33:30.220 --> 00:33:32.280
Dishwater, face to the gutter.

00:33:37.600 --> 00:33:42.620
For 40 years, I have been asking you to give me medium boiled eggs.

00:33:42.880 --> 00:33:44.540
Are these medium boiled?

00:33:44.900 --> 00:33:45.780
They are not.

00:33:46.500 --> 00:33:51.030
They are in the same fluid and virginal state as when they left the hen.

00:33:58.080 --> 00:33:59.680
You've been messing this paper about.

00:34:00.600 --> 00:34:02.400
But you're trying to do the crossword puzzle.

00:34:03.060 --> 00:34:06.480
I don't read your paper. I have my own, and you know it.

00:34:07.290 --> 00:34:09.470
Altogether, I know too much about you.

00:34:10.960 --> 00:34:12.340
Then I'd better go altogether.

00:34:13.290 --> 00:34:16.490
That is exactly what I wanted to tell you.

00:34:25.190 --> 00:34:26.130
Good morning, Miss Leslie.

00:34:26.470 --> 00:34:28.780
Good morning. What's the matter, Jeffress?

00:34:28.880 --> 00:34:29.980
Miss Lordship's just given me...

00:34:30.840 --> 00:34:33.610
Oh, come along, he's just taking his cigars.

00:34:38.100 --> 00:34:38.740
Morning, Grandpa.

00:34:39.020 --> 00:34:40.650
Leslie, where have you been?

00:34:40.790 --> 00:34:41.750
Captain Jeffries told you.

00:34:42.430 --> 00:34:43.590
I most certainly did tell you.

00:34:43.750 --> 00:34:44.270
Oh, there you go.

00:34:44.700 --> 00:34:46.940
You know perfectly well there was a fog last night,

00:34:47.580 --> 00:34:49.700
and Miss Leslie spent the night at the Royal Parks Hotel.

00:34:49.980 --> 00:34:51.580
Her father and mother are in India,

00:34:51.800 --> 00:34:53.200
and I'm responsible for her.

00:34:53.260 --> 00:34:53.720
So am I.

00:34:53.920 --> 00:34:56.310
You? I'm her grandfather.

00:34:56.820 --> 00:34:57.740
Seems I know her better.

00:34:58.190 --> 00:34:59.970
Well, I'm appalled to think that my grand...

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.140
should leave this house at 9 in the evening

00:35:02.140 --> 00:35:03.900
and return at 9 in the morning.

00:35:04.460 --> 00:35:06.860
You know perfectly well there are some girls you can't trust

00:35:06.860 --> 00:35:07.980
to go out and post a letter.

00:35:08.510 --> 00:35:10.190
But Miss Leslie, you can trust to go to the North Pole.

00:35:10.430 --> 00:35:13.650
Isn't it my duty to ask her for a full account of her goings?

00:35:14.310 --> 00:35:14.910
Full account?

00:35:15.940 --> 00:35:17.720
You're not a crying and meddlesome judge.

00:35:18.390 --> 00:35:19.570
You're an adoring grandpa.

00:35:22.370 --> 00:35:22.810
Grandpa?

00:35:23.130 --> 00:35:23.650
Yes, darling?

00:35:24.340 --> 00:35:25.760
Do you know a man called Logan?

00:35:26.560 --> 00:35:27.000
Logan?

00:35:27.500 --> 00:35:28.800
Logan Everard.

00:35:28.800 --> 00:35:29.680
That was a report.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:30.740
Where's the second?

00:35:32.580 --> 00:35:32.980
Logan.

00:35:33.550 --> 00:35:35.050
Yeah, he'll be in my court today.

00:35:35.870 --> 00:35:36.270
Will he?

00:35:36.590 --> 00:35:36.770
Mm-hmm.

00:35:37.110 --> 00:35:37.510
Glendon.

00:35:38.090 --> 00:35:38.830
What's he like, Grandpa?

00:35:39.380 --> 00:35:39.780
Logan.

00:35:40.550 --> 00:35:42.510
Oh, he's a good cross-examiner.

00:35:42.810 --> 00:35:44.930
Oh, but a wretched fisherman.

00:35:46.120 --> 00:35:47.040
Why do you ask?

00:35:47.590 --> 00:35:48.470
I think he'll marry me.

00:35:49.720 --> 00:35:50.300
He propose?

00:35:50.750 --> 00:35:51.130
Oh, no.

00:35:51.330 --> 00:35:53.800
He doesn't know about it yet.

00:35:55.120 --> 00:35:57.040
Well, if he didn't know about it, how'd he?

00:35:58.100 --> 00:35:58.460
Leslie!

00:36:00.160 --> 00:36:01.240
What on earth are you wearing?

00:36:01.800 --> 00:36:03.400
Bad teeth, aren't they? They're his pajamas.

00:36:04.040 --> 00:36:04.320
Whose?

00:36:05.140 --> 00:36:05.540
Logan's.

00:36:05.800 --> 00:36:10.120
How comes that you're wearing the pajamas of a man whose existence yesterday you knew nothing?

00:36:10.500 --> 00:36:11.500
I slept in his bed.

00:36:11.760 --> 00:36:12.120
What?

00:36:13.620 --> 00:36:14.980
Well, you see, he has two beds.

00:36:15.300 --> 00:36:18.850
So we transported number two into the sitting room and I slept in number one.

00:36:19.110 --> 00:36:20.630
Leslie, this is the limit.

00:36:21.110 --> 00:36:22.910
Didn't I tell you Miss Leslie was all right?

00:36:23.470 --> 00:36:25.010
You don't understand the new generation.

00:36:25.190 --> 00:36:27.310
No, I don't think anybody else does either.

00:36:27.900 --> 00:36:28.280
Grandpa?

00:36:28.620 --> 00:36:29.000
Yes, dear?

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:31.480
He doesn't know who?

00:36:31.620 --> 00:36:31.760
Who?

00:36:33.910 --> 00:36:34.950
He thought I was a woman.

00:36:35.520 --> 00:36:36.600
And a very wicked woman.

00:36:37.440 --> 00:36:38.720
Not much like a woman.

00:36:38.960 --> 00:36:40.540
Certainly not like a wicked woman.

00:36:41.170 --> 00:36:42.330
But I behaved like one.

00:36:43.410 --> 00:36:45.670
And he thought this ridiculous thing and thought I was married.

00:36:46.090 --> 00:36:47.610
He's a blockhead.

00:36:49.800 --> 00:36:50.500
He is not.

00:36:51.090 --> 00:36:56.250
If a slip of a girl in the ring can deceive a man, he must be a dunce.

00:36:56.960 --> 00:36:59.960
Jeffries, did it never happen when you were...

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:03.340
You're a little younger that Grandpa was led up the garden path by a girl?

00:37:03.620 --> 00:37:04.040
Never.

00:37:04.800 --> 00:37:08.780
And you're a wise and great judge now.

00:37:08.980 --> 00:37:11.440
And so will Logan be one day, given it was time.

00:37:12.040 --> 00:37:13.440
And then no one will be able to fool him.

00:37:13.710 --> 00:37:14.670
How much time?

00:37:15.290 --> 00:37:17.210
Oh, 40 or 50 years.

00:37:19.010 --> 00:37:23.060
Oh, you take that notice I gave you seriously?

00:37:23.470 --> 00:37:26.080
No, milord. Good boy.

00:37:40.750 --> 00:37:41.630
Good morning, Mr. Logan.

00:37:41.870 --> 00:37:43.540
Morning, Diane. Thank you, Tom.

00:37:44.150 --> 00:37:45.170
Welcome back to London.

00:37:45.290 --> 00:37:45.670
Thank you.

00:37:46.720 --> 00:37:47.360
Sweet little town.

00:37:47.960 --> 00:37:49.140
Except for the weather, of course.

00:37:49.300 --> 00:37:49.920
What's the matter with it?

00:37:50.560 --> 00:37:51.940
London weather's the best in the world.

00:37:52.560 --> 00:37:54.000
Last night's pond, for example.

00:37:54.180 --> 00:37:54.480
Exactly.

00:37:55.110 --> 00:37:56.630
Where else would you find such a phenomenon?

00:37:57.760 --> 00:37:59.960
Finest city in the world dons an impenetrable...

00:38:01.160 --> 00:38:02.800
Life becomes an enthralling adventure.

00:38:03.580 --> 00:38:06.560
Fate guides your footsteps that at any moment you might meet a miracle.

00:38:07.760 --> 00:38:09.640
I see. Then you did meet the miracle.

00:38:10.400 --> 00:38:11.320
Keep that alone.

00:38:13.550 --> 00:38:17.250
Strictly speaking, you're always in the habit of meeting miracles, fog or no fog.

00:38:17.590 --> 00:38:20.340
And if I might say a word upon that subject,

00:38:21.150 --> 00:38:24.410
isn't it about time you stopped these encounters with miracle after miracle?

00:38:24.810 --> 00:38:27.470
He knows me, my dear fellow, member of my club.

00:38:27.490 --> 00:38:27.610
What?

00:38:29.260 --> 00:38:29.500
Mir.

00:38:31.050 --> 00:38:31.310
Myr.

00:38:32.260 --> 00:38:33.760
Lord Myr, yes, yes. How do you do?

00:38:33.880 --> 00:38:35.900
How are you, my dear chap? How are you? Terribly well.

00:38:36.410 --> 00:38:38.130
Don't ask me. I'm terribly unwell.

00:38:38.290 --> 00:38:38.630
What's the trouble?

00:38:38.980 --> 00:38:40.810
Trouble? Trouble?

00:38:41.480 --> 00:38:42.060
My wife.

00:38:42.540 --> 00:38:43.780
What's the trouble with Lady Myr?

00:38:44.180 --> 00:38:45.960
Trouble? She's just spent the night with a man.

00:38:46.780 --> 00:38:49.440
Isn't that trouble enough here? Isn't that grounds for divorce?

00:38:49.640 --> 00:38:50.760
It's enough for any court in the world.

00:38:50.900 --> 00:38:53.240
But the correct procedure is to see your solicitor.

00:38:53.240 --> 00:38:54.460
It is. I know the correct procedure.

00:38:54.560 --> 00:38:57.720
But a fellow at the club told me that you can dissolve a marriage as quickly as an aspirin tablet.

00:38:57.840 --> 00:38:59.880
So before going to any solicitor, chap, I want your advice.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:02.480
Yes, well, I'm rather busy, so if you'll give me the essential facts...

00:39:02.480 --> 00:39:04.240
I'll give you the essentials. You've spent the night with it.

00:39:04.240 --> 00:39:07.510
Yes, yes, I know. But do you love her?

00:39:08.220 --> 00:39:14.620
Well, yes. Why do you want to divorce her?

00:39:14.740 --> 00:39:17.440
Well, dash it all, though, but one can't afford to be made a fool of, can one?

00:39:17.740 --> 00:39:18.740
After all, of our limits.

00:39:19.000 --> 00:39:20.540
Yes, I understand you perfectly, Lord Mayor.

00:39:21.600 --> 00:39:24.520
I've given you a wife, your name, your fortune, and your devoted love.

00:39:25.300 --> 00:39:27.460
She, in return, has given you the anguish of humiliation.

00:39:27.890 --> 00:39:29.670
That's it. You have it exactly, my dear fellow.

00:39:31.310 --> 00:39:32.750
I've heard the same story too many times.

00:39:33.810 --> 00:39:35.450
The adoring husband of a cheating wife.

00:39:36.400 --> 00:39:37.180
What evidence have you?

00:39:37.360 --> 00:39:39.180
Last night, she left the house before dinner

00:39:39.180 --> 00:39:41.120
and didn't return until 9 o'clock this morning.

00:39:41.260 --> 00:39:42.100
Suspicious in itself.

00:39:42.220 --> 00:39:44.540
Then, there's the eyewitness testimony of the maid

00:39:44.540 --> 00:39:46.580
who went to the hotel and saw her emerging...

00:39:46.580 --> 00:39:47.380
What hotel was it?

00:39:47.980 --> 00:39:48.700
The Royal Parks.

00:39:51.670 --> 00:39:52.030
What did you say?

00:39:52.420 --> 00:39:52.980
The Royal Parks.

00:39:53.060 --> 00:39:53.920
I dare say you saw in the paper,

00:39:53.980 --> 00:39:55.680
there was a costume ball given there last night.

00:39:55.820 --> 00:39:56.500
A charity affair.

00:39:56.800 --> 00:39:56.960
Aha!

00:39:57.710 --> 00:39:58.070
Charity.

00:39:58.630 --> 00:39:59.910
Yes, yes, I heard something.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:04.760
Now, there's another very significant point. She was out all night and in fancy dress.

00:40:05.080 --> 00:40:06.400
Can you wonder if I'm being a bit upset?

00:40:06.710 --> 00:40:08.390
No, no, no, I don't wonder at all.

00:40:08.640 --> 00:40:11.260
But tell me, what sort of a costume did she wear?

00:40:11.420 --> 00:40:13.100
I don't see the costume has any bearing on the matter.

00:40:13.340 --> 00:40:15.780
Oh, yes, it has. For instance, if she'd been dressed as a deep sea diver,

00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:17.240
wouldn't it be easier if I could...

00:40:17.240 --> 00:40:19.420
Ah, but she wasn't. Trouncingly beautiful.

00:40:19.560 --> 00:40:21.500
She was dressed as a French lady of the Second Empire.

00:40:21.800 --> 00:40:23.980
You know, the Empress Eugénie, crinolines, that sort of thing.

00:40:25.300 --> 00:40:25.480
Yes.

00:40:26.500 --> 00:40:27.760
There was a very heavy fog last night.

00:40:27.940 --> 00:40:28.580
Yes, I was conscious.

00:40:29.320 --> 00:40:29.960
I couldn't have...

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:33.270
I told him my wife to the ball. Like a fool, I went to a banquet, you know, an old regiment.

00:40:33.520 --> 00:40:34.440
Good chap's bad food.

00:40:34.660 --> 00:40:36.620
Yes, yes, yes. Get on with it, please. What happened?

00:40:36.820 --> 00:40:39.520
She spent the night at the hotel, but not alone.

00:40:40.750 --> 00:40:41.810
How do you know? From Saunders.

00:40:42.070 --> 00:40:42.970
Who's Saunders? Her maid.

00:40:43.130 --> 00:40:43.590
How does she know?

00:40:44.290 --> 00:40:46.290
Because she went to the hotel with some clothes.

00:40:46.620 --> 00:40:47.580
Did your wife ask for the clothes?

00:40:47.680 --> 00:40:51.760
She did not. She just telephoned about nine o'clock to say that she was coming home presently, but I sent Saunders.

00:40:52.110 --> 00:40:56.650
And Saunders heard from the corridor of the hotel that she was talking in her room with a man.

00:40:57.320 --> 00:40:58.020
Did Saunders go in?

00:40:58.260 --> 00:40:59.960
Saunders did not. She's clever and loyal. She listened.

00:41:01.240 --> 00:41:01.780
What does she hear?

00:41:02.270 --> 00:41:06.600
She saw, she saw my wife emerging from the room at about a quarter to nine,

00:41:06.840 --> 00:41:09.300
and she saw a man come out of the same room after her.

00:41:14.490 --> 00:41:16.050
And then what? Isn't that enough for you?

00:41:17.800 --> 00:41:18.100
Enough?

00:41:19.770 --> 00:41:21.670
You have the audacity to bring against your wife,

00:41:21.860 --> 00:41:23.920
the most serious charge that can be brought against a woman,

00:41:24.080 --> 00:41:26.800
and you expect me to mobilize the law against a superb woman

00:41:26.800 --> 00:41:29.390
on the grounds of Saunders listening at her door?

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:32.460
Quarter to nine, fancy dress and a strange young man.

00:41:32.600 --> 00:41:33.840
What, you mean you refuse my case?

00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:35.800
There is no case. I refuse it indignantly.

00:41:36.040 --> 00:41:37.200
You'll only listen to Saunders.

00:41:37.320 --> 00:41:39.240
I don't wish to listen to Saunders. I've heard quite enough.

00:41:39.380 --> 00:41:42.300
From all that you've said, Lord Mayor, I've gained a very clear picture of your wife.

00:41:43.300 --> 00:41:47.170
A noble woman, fearless, devoted, pure in heart.

00:41:47.290 --> 00:41:50.680
Not at all the type of woman that would do anything to dismerge the family discussion.

00:41:51.000 --> 00:41:52.160
Well, what about my humiliation?

00:41:52.300 --> 00:41:53.420
You took her for better or worse, didn't you?

00:41:53.520 --> 00:41:55.400
And she promised to love, honor and obey.

00:41:55.560 --> 00:41:59.460
Yeah. Think back to that sacred ceremony. There she stood.

00:42:00.030 --> 00:42:03.640
An innocent girl, about to face the most perilous moment in her life.

00:42:03.930 --> 00:42:06.590
Look here, Logan, you've got this slightly mixed. She was not an innocent girl.

00:42:07.020 --> 00:42:11.080
Before she married me, she was divorced from a fellow called Lauderdale, who trains racehorses.

00:42:14.130 --> 00:42:14.230
Oh.

00:42:14.880 --> 00:42:16.140
Ah-ha, I make her say, oh, again.

00:42:16.660 --> 00:42:19.720
Before she married Lauderdale, she was divorced from the Baron de Brissac,

00:42:19.960 --> 00:42:21.840
who makes an inferior grain of brandy.

00:42:22.740 --> 00:42:23.440
She's a French woman?

00:42:23.600 --> 00:42:24.080
An American.

00:42:24.760 --> 00:42:27.280
Her first husband was called Wild Man Cavanaugh,

00:42:27.620 --> 00:42:29.880
a professional wrestler by trade. She got rid of him at Reno.

00:42:32.400 --> 00:42:32.990
It seems impossible.

00:42:34.880 --> 00:42:35.820
Foreign manager, isn't she?

00:42:35.820 --> 00:42:36.420
She's so young.

00:42:36.910 --> 00:42:37.830
Who said she was so young?

00:42:38.620 --> 00:42:39.810
Uh, you did, didn't you?

00:42:40.030 --> 00:42:40.230
Aha!

00:42:40.430 --> 00:42:42.980
As a matter of fact, she looks young, entrancingly so.

00:42:43.410 --> 00:42:44.330
She's a serpent, Logan.

00:42:44.930 --> 00:42:47.800
Viper coils herself about the heart of innocent men

00:42:47.800 --> 00:42:50.960
and then strikes rid of her or face serpent ruin.

00:42:52.720 --> 00:42:53.900
Begin to see your point, love me.

00:42:54.190 --> 00:42:54.630
Good fellow.

00:42:54.870 --> 00:42:55.630
Then you'll take my case.

00:42:55.750 --> 00:42:57.720
Well, I shall think it over then.

00:42:58.520 --> 00:42:59.500
That's all I can say just now.

00:43:00.350 --> 00:43:04.470
I told you I was very busy. I'll call you later in the day.

00:43:05.130 --> 00:43:06.010
Very busy day.

00:43:07.580 --> 00:43:08.060
Yes, huh?

00:43:15.140 --> 00:43:19.310
Horse been a brandy dealer and a wrestler.

00:43:24.590 --> 00:43:25.150
What's the matter with you?

00:43:26.740 --> 00:43:27.560
Do you know who that was in here?

00:43:27.800 --> 00:43:29.970
Yes, Lord Mere. Everybody knows.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:32.020
Was him one of the best shots in the army?

00:43:32.350 --> 00:43:32.990
Oh, is he really?

00:43:34.490 --> 00:43:36.230
Well, that costume belongs to his wife.

00:43:36.450 --> 00:43:38.890
What? So the miracle's identified.

00:43:39.250 --> 00:43:39.990
Lady Meir.

00:43:40.850 --> 00:43:41.590
Oh, please don't whistle.

00:43:41.750 --> 00:43:43.570
You have got yourself into a nice mess now.

00:43:44.200 --> 00:43:47.100
How are you going to stand up in court and blaggard correspondents

00:43:47.100 --> 00:43:48.760
for doing exactly what you've been doing yourself?

00:43:48.980 --> 00:43:51.210
Look here, Slade. That's the dreadful part of it.

00:43:51.360 --> 00:43:52.780
I didn't do anything.

00:43:53.180 --> 00:43:55.840
Oh, and what would you say to a correspondent who told you that?

00:43:56.080 --> 00:43:57.600
But it's true, I tell you. I swear to you.

00:43:58.080 --> 00:43:58.740
Nothing happens.

00:44:00.250 --> 00:44:06.490
All right, go ahead and swear, but, Mr. Logan, do you expect me to believe that nothing happened?

00:44:08.930 --> 00:44:14.680
Do you expect me to believe that nothing...

00:44:15.730 --> 00:44:23.360
Well, that is, you see, well, nothing of any consequence, if you get what I mean.

00:44:23.600 --> 00:44:25.200
Oh, yes, yes, I get what you mean.

00:44:26.460 --> 00:44:27.760
So I've no doubt, Mrs. Lordship.

00:44:28.080 --> 00:44:29.980
I'm afraid I should prefer an...

00:44:30.980 --> 00:44:35.760
Any explanation, Mrs. Johnson? Can you explain to his Lordship what you mean?

00:44:36.000 --> 00:44:42.420
We have ample opportunities in this court for learning what women mean,

00:44:43.180 --> 00:44:46.400
or what they mean they mean, if in these days they mean anything at all.

00:44:49.130 --> 00:44:53.170
There is one very simple explanation of this case.

00:44:53.410 --> 00:44:59.980
Mrs. Johnson is a woman, and he's scarce to remind your Lordship.

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:04.950
That woman has a religion of her own, the ancient creed of womanhood.

00:45:06.090 --> 00:45:11.140
It contains only one article of faith, but every woman sincerely and steadfastly believes in it.

00:45:12.160 --> 00:45:15.860
And that is that she is the unique and perfect achievement of the human species.

00:45:16.800 --> 00:45:24.220
A being especially evolved to be above criticism, beyond reproach, and outside the law.

00:45:24.980 --> 00:45:28.840
Man in his folly and kindness has been bamboozled into accepting woman as a rational being

00:45:28.840 --> 00:45:29.960
and has granted her emancipation.

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:31.540
on that assumption. What is his reward?

00:45:32.550 --> 00:45:34.170
Modern woman has disowned womanhood

00:45:34.170 --> 00:45:35.790
but refuses man's obligation.

00:45:37.080 --> 00:45:39.540
She demands freedom but won't accept responsibility.

00:45:40.560 --> 00:45:43.020
She insists upon time to develop her personality

00:45:43.020 --> 00:45:45.160
and she spends it in cogitating

00:45:45.160 --> 00:45:47.200
on which part of her body to paint next.

00:45:51.080 --> 00:45:52.160
And she means idleness.

00:45:52.890 --> 00:45:55.910
By equality, she means carrying on like Catherine the Great.

00:45:56.300 --> 00:45:58.860
Uh, carry on like who, Mr. Logan?

00:45:59.620 --> 00:45:59.980
Catherine the...

00:46:01.700 --> 00:46:03.820
Carry on like Catherine the Great.

00:46:04.840 --> 00:46:05.860
Oh, thank you.

00:46:07.000 --> 00:46:10.360
By companionship with man, she means that he should wait upon her hand and foot.

00:46:10.540 --> 00:46:13.560
A woman has no loyalty, decency or justice.

00:46:14.170 --> 00:46:16.030
No endurance, reticence or self-control.

00:46:16.480 --> 00:46:18.440
No affection, fine feelings or mercy.

00:46:18.900 --> 00:46:21.460
In short, she is unprincipled, relentless and exacting.

00:46:21.960 --> 00:46:23.700
Idle, unproductive and tedious.

00:46:24.290 --> 00:46:25.570
Unimaginative, humorless and vain.

00:46:25.790 --> 00:46:27.110
Vindictive, undignified and weak.

00:46:27.250 --> 00:46:29.790
And the sooner man takes out his whip again, the better for sanity and progress.

00:46:30.060 --> 00:46:33.240
That is the explanation of Mrs. Johnson, and that is the explanation of this case.

00:46:33.440 --> 00:46:34.240
You may stand up.

00:46:48.610 --> 00:46:50.340
You mustn't be happy to Mr. Logan.

00:46:50.600 --> 00:46:52.740
He'll ask you some questions. You must reply to them too.

00:46:53.630 --> 00:46:55.430
I know, but whatever Lady Mere...

00:46:55.580 --> 00:46:57.540
Whatever Lady Mere thinks, no harm will come to you.

00:47:01.470 --> 00:47:05.310
Lord Mears here. He's got a solicitor with him and the principal witness, Saunders, the maid.

00:47:05.720 --> 00:47:07.440
But I can't let her see me. She was the hotel.

00:47:07.680 --> 00:47:09.500
Well, you're going to be caught some time. It may as well be now.

00:47:09.700 --> 00:47:10.120
Oh, no, no, my judge.

00:47:10.980 --> 00:47:11.600
Go right here.

00:47:12.160 --> 00:47:15.260
Ah, Logan, I thought I heard your voice. Now, this is Hallflower, my solicitor.

00:47:15.320 --> 00:47:16.300
You know each other, don't you?

00:47:16.320 --> 00:47:16.880
Good morning, Logan.

00:47:17.180 --> 00:47:18.720
And this is Saunders that I told you about.

00:47:19.260 --> 00:47:20.740
How do you do? Please sit there.

00:47:21.120 --> 00:47:23.860
Have you any further doubts about my case? Saunders will dispel.

00:47:24.990 --> 00:47:26.520
Saunders, you saw the man, didn't you?

00:47:26.700 --> 00:47:27.660
I did, my lord.

00:47:27.820 --> 00:47:28.800
And you've never seen him before.

00:47:30.160 --> 00:47:31.700
Well, I'm not, I'm not sure, my lord.

00:47:31.960 --> 00:47:33.950
You're not sure? You can't have seen it very clearly.

00:47:34.490 --> 00:47:36.150
I didn't have my glasses on, sir.

00:47:36.800 --> 00:47:38.240
Ah, then you wouldn't be able to recognize him, would you?

00:47:38.460 --> 00:47:39.560
Oh, I didn't say that, sir.

00:47:39.760 --> 00:47:41.780
I didn't say I wouldn't recognize him.

00:47:41.940 --> 00:47:43.820
I said I didn't recognize him.

00:47:44.560 --> 00:47:45.780
Very intelligent, old boy.

00:47:46.400 --> 00:47:49.540
Now, Saunders, just tell Mr. Logan what you saw described to me.

00:47:50.520 --> 00:47:53.420
Oh, well, my lord, I don't know that I could describe him.

00:47:53.660 --> 00:47:55.020
Ah, you may try.

00:47:55.690 --> 00:47:58.130
Well, um, well, I don't quite know what to say.

00:47:58.370 --> 00:47:59.970
He was just an ordinary, commonplace...

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:00.740
a sort of man?

00:48:01.660 --> 00:48:03.360
Scribe the man. Details. Details, woman.

00:48:03.600 --> 00:48:04.660
No, no, no. Don't be impatient.

00:48:04.760 --> 00:48:06.880
Give the poor girl a chance now, Saunders.

00:48:06.980 --> 00:48:07.960
Just you don't be afraid.

00:48:08.240 --> 00:48:09.640
Just tell Mr. Logan exactly.

00:48:09.860 --> 00:48:11.260
Was he tall or short?

00:48:12.160 --> 00:48:15.800
Oh, he was just about ordinary height.

00:48:16.400 --> 00:48:18.520
Oh, is he dark, fair, or ginger?

00:48:19.380 --> 00:48:20.980
He was what you might call medium.

00:48:21.660 --> 00:48:23.260
Was he young, old?

00:48:23.680 --> 00:48:25.360
Well, he was what you might call...

00:48:25.360 --> 00:48:26.970
Medium. Medium, that's right.

00:48:27.450 --> 00:48:28.590
Is he clean shaven?

00:48:29.570 --> 00:48:29.970
Well...

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:30.120
No.

00:48:30.500 --> 00:48:33.030
Had he got a beard?

00:48:33.550 --> 00:48:34.370
Oh, no, my lord, no.

00:48:34.490 --> 00:48:35.850
No, I'm quite positive about that.

00:48:35.910 --> 00:48:36.650
He hadn't got a beard.

00:48:37.480 --> 00:48:39.160
He might have had a small moustache, though.

00:48:39.630 --> 00:48:39.830
Ah!

00:48:40.380 --> 00:48:41.020
He had a moustache.

00:48:41.310 --> 00:48:41.530
No.

00:48:41.840 --> 00:48:42.300
No, he didn't.

00:48:43.320 --> 00:48:46.780
Well, at any event, you're quite sure that you've never seen him before or since?

00:48:46.920 --> 00:48:47.440
Oh, quite, quite.

00:48:48.070 --> 00:48:48.490
What is it?

00:48:48.690 --> 00:48:50.780
The lady is here, sir.

00:48:51.930 --> 00:48:52.710
What lady?

00:48:53.230 --> 00:48:54.190
The lady in the case.

00:48:55.770 --> 00:48:57.290
The lady in the...

00:48:57.860 --> 00:48:58.160
Ah!

00:48:58.860 --> 00:48:59.550
Excuse me.

00:49:04.640 --> 00:49:09.440
Well, what have you, what have you come here for?

00:49:10.120 --> 00:49:11.720
Return these, your pajamas.

00:49:12.740 --> 00:49:13.040
Thank you.

00:49:13.220 --> 00:49:16.500
Anything else?

00:49:18.770 --> 00:49:19.570
What's happened to you?

00:49:20.190 --> 00:49:21.850
You're not nearly as sweet as you were at breakfast.

00:49:22.390 --> 00:49:23.170
I'll tell you what's happened.

00:49:23.760 --> 00:49:25.040
Your husband's in there.

00:49:26.860 --> 00:49:27.100
Who?

00:49:29.060 --> 00:49:29.980
Oh, I don't blame you at all.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:34.380
for being so confused after all the husbands you have to look back on but this isn't the horse

00:49:34.380 --> 00:49:40.240
trainer or the brandy dealer or the wrestler this happens to be your latest lord mere lord mere yes

00:49:40.240 --> 00:49:47.430
that's the one and who told you he was my husband he did he told me everything and you'll be just as

00:49:47.430 --> 00:49:51.210
unpleasantly surprised as i was to learn how very much he does know he knows all about the royal

00:49:51.870 --> 00:49:52.650
And the costume.

00:49:54.540 --> 00:49:55.560
What does he want of you?

00:49:56.500 --> 00:49:56.840
Divorce.

00:49:57.230 --> 00:49:57.570
Divorce.

00:49:57.790 --> 00:49:58.130
Divorce.

00:49:58.130 --> 00:49:58.230
Divorce.

00:50:00.860 --> 00:50:02.100
Lord Mayor wants a divorce.

00:50:02.430 --> 00:50:03.070
Very interesting.

00:50:03.760 --> 00:50:04.400
Yes, isn't it?

00:50:04.840 --> 00:50:06.240
And you're going to help him get it, I hope.

00:50:07.090 --> 00:50:09.030
Help him to divorce you when I'm the correspondent?

00:50:11.200 --> 00:50:11.600
Oh, yes.

00:50:11.700 --> 00:50:14.200
I can understand you being so callous with all your experience.

00:50:14.340 --> 00:50:15.640
But let me tell you, it'll mean ruin to me.

00:50:16.220 --> 00:50:16.540
Ruin?

00:50:17.840 --> 00:50:20.450
I can just imagine what Lord Steele would say about it.

00:50:21.930 --> 00:50:22.650
Lord Steele?

00:50:23.270 --> 00:50:25.310
Yes, all the judges I have to face, he's the nastiest.

00:50:26.980 --> 00:50:27.660
Joyce, my disgrace.

00:50:30.220 --> 00:50:35.090
But, um, if Lord Mayor gets what he wants, then I'll be free.

00:50:35.470 --> 00:50:38.070
You and I could, so to speak, get together.

00:50:39.940 --> 00:50:41.220
You'd like that, wouldn't you?

00:50:42.200 --> 00:50:44.940
At the expense of my career, a few pleasures?

00:50:46.050 --> 00:50:48.080
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:50:49.050 --> 00:50:51.310
I thought you were beginning to be rather fond of me.

00:50:52.240 --> 00:50:55.120
I know, um, I know I couldn't help liking you,

00:50:55.240 --> 00:50:57.080
even though you were rather unpleasant at first.

00:50:58.740 --> 00:50:59.980
But, I suppose...

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:08.520
There's nothing left for me but to take my medicine and go.

00:51:12.930 --> 00:51:15.030
I can certainly understand how you've trapped all those men.

00:51:17.440 --> 00:51:18.000
Oh, what men?

00:51:19.110 --> 00:51:21.470
Lordsdale, the Baron de Brissac,

00:51:23.440 --> 00:51:24.620
Wild Man, somebody or other.

00:51:25.120 --> 00:51:26.680
Oh, oh, those?

00:51:27.690 --> 00:51:28.440
Yes, those.

00:51:30.160 --> 00:51:34.330
And then, poor Lord Mere, now me.

00:51:40.170 --> 00:51:44.960
Yes, I shouldn't admit it. I love you.

00:51:47.620 --> 00:51:52.090
Even now, now that I know the horrible truth, I'm wild about you.

00:51:54.990 --> 00:51:55.950
Want to take you in my arms?

00:51:57.070 --> 00:51:57.770
Then why don't you?

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:12.810
What am I doing standing here kissing you?

00:52:12.950 --> 00:52:14.610
And doing it very well, if I may say so.

00:52:14.730 --> 00:52:19.810
When your husband is in there, and his solicitor, and Saunders, who saw us both, wait here.

00:52:25.600 --> 00:52:28.920
Now think, Saunders. Think, you know, just think. Don't be a fool, Saunders.

00:52:30.220 --> 00:52:43.410
Yes, now, now, now, now, now, now, now, now, now, now, now, now, now, now, now, now, so tell me, you say you wouldn't recognize this man's face at all?

00:52:43.590 --> 00:52:46.290
No, sir, no, I think I know his walk, sir.

00:52:48.310 --> 00:52:51.850
Yes, but you, you've never seen him before or since?

00:52:52.130 --> 00:52:56.470
No, sir, no, but I've known all the other gentlemen that we had since we got our first divorce in Reno.

00:52:56.730 --> 00:52:59.970
Saunders has been the faithful maid of my wife ever since her first marriage, haven't you, Saunders?

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:01.460
Yes, my lord. Five years.

00:53:01.820 --> 00:53:04.230
Five years? You've established world records, haven't you?

00:53:04.790 --> 00:53:07.630
Now then, after the divorce in Reno came the marriage with the Baron de Brisa.

00:53:07.890 --> 00:53:11.050
No, sir, no. After Mr. Kavanagh came Mr. Miller.

00:53:11.500 --> 00:53:11.760
Mr. Miller?

00:53:12.140 --> 00:53:13.320
Oh, well...

00:53:13.410 --> 00:53:15.690
Yes, yes. Well, I don't think there are all these details in this.

00:53:15.850 --> 00:53:18.930
I'm very sorry, Lord Mayor, but if you want me to handle this case, I must hear every detail.

00:53:19.740 --> 00:53:23.560
Yes, you only do yourself harm if you... if you hide anything from your doctor or your lawyer.

00:53:24.020 --> 00:53:24.200
Great.

00:53:26.640 --> 00:53:27.500
Now then, after Mr. Miller.

00:53:28.120 --> 00:53:28.960
Mr. Van Hoon?

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:30.760
After Mr. Van Houten?

00:53:32.020 --> 00:53:32.740
Barron, please, sir.

00:53:33.380 --> 00:53:34.400
How long till the divorce?

00:53:35.100 --> 00:53:36.000
Fourteen months, sir.

00:53:36.500 --> 00:53:36.900
Fourteen months.

00:53:37.000 --> 00:53:37.900
And after the barron, please, sir?

00:53:39.100 --> 00:53:39.560
Mr. Miller.

00:53:41.170 --> 00:53:42.530
Mr. Miller came after Mr. Cameron?

00:53:42.830 --> 00:53:43.530
No, sir, no.

00:53:43.710 --> 00:53:45.210
That was Mr. Miller the first, sir.

00:53:45.350 --> 00:53:46.590
This is Mr. Miller the second.

00:53:47.290 --> 00:53:47.450
Oh.

00:53:48.510 --> 00:53:49.510
Is there a Mr. Miller the third?

00:53:49.710 --> 00:53:50.410
No, sir, no.

00:53:50.570 --> 00:53:52.870
Only Senor Mendoza from the Argentine,

00:53:52.990 --> 00:53:54.710
and then Mr. Lauderdale,

00:53:54.890 --> 00:53:56.560
and then his lordship, sir.

00:53:58.700 --> 00:53:59.020
Sailing?

00:53:59.650 --> 00:53:59.970
Well...

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:00.700
I've got all you want.

00:54:01.060 --> 00:54:01.420
Yes?

00:54:01.680 --> 00:54:02.760
Will you undertake my case?

00:54:03.490 --> 00:54:04.230
Yes, I will.

00:54:04.810 --> 00:54:06.550
My friend Holfry will prepare it for me.

00:54:07.270 --> 00:54:08.710
And I will get your divorce for you.

00:54:08.790 --> 00:54:09.210
Good lad.

00:54:09.450 --> 00:54:09.990
Now, come along.

00:54:11.900 --> 00:54:12.280
Is you...

00:54:12.340 --> 00:54:15.420
You're sure you're not worried about us not knowing the man at the Royal Parks Hotel?

00:54:16.360 --> 00:54:18.220
I know the man at the Royal Parks Hotel.

00:54:18.550 --> 00:54:18.770
What?

00:54:19.660 --> 00:54:21.300
That is, I know the kind of fellow he must have been.

00:54:21.920 --> 00:54:23.980
After Mr. Miller the first and Mr. Miller the second.

00:54:24.710 --> 00:54:26.310
Senor Mendoza from the Argentine.

00:54:27.460 --> 00:54:28.520
He looks like being a fofu.

00:54:28.740 --> 00:54:29.140
Good afternoon.

00:54:42.510 --> 00:54:42.890
What is she?

00:54:43.580 --> 00:54:44.200
Ooh, mythical?

00:54:44.740 --> 00:54:45.060
Gone.

00:55:31.530 --> 00:55:32.750
I've decided to take on the case.

00:55:33.280 --> 00:55:34.440
You've decided to face scandal?

00:55:34.520 --> 00:55:34.800
Yes.

00:55:35.620 --> 00:55:35.960
Ruined?

00:55:36.060 --> 00:55:36.300
Yes.

00:55:37.430 --> 00:55:41.400
And the reason for the sudden courage is because Thorn is a short-sighted and you think you're safe?

00:55:41.500 --> 00:55:42.380
One's never safe in a case.

00:55:42.890 --> 00:55:43.690
And why take it on?

00:55:43.950 --> 00:55:45.870
Because I hope that you will marry me when you are free.

00:55:48.340 --> 00:55:48.600
Will you?

00:56:01.660 --> 00:56:27.060
It was somewhere in the back of your mind when you came to see me.

00:56:28.550 --> 00:56:28.930
It might have been.

00:56:30.030 --> 00:56:33.180
I didn't like you in your office. I much preferred you in your bedroom.

00:56:34.280 --> 00:56:34.660
My bedroom?

00:56:36.040 --> 00:56:36.540
My bedroom.

00:56:37.200 --> 00:56:39.260
Surely that's the proper place to judge your future husband.

00:56:40.450 --> 00:56:42.830
Aren't you frightened any more of the hectic years of my past?

00:56:56.400 --> 00:56:56.740
Yeah, I miss.

00:56:57.450 --> 00:56:59.230
As a matter of fact, I don't feel old at all.

00:57:01.500 --> 00:57:05.910
Sometimes when you smile at me, I feel that you're as guileless and innocent as a child.

00:57:06.410 --> 00:57:07.650
That's why I smile at you.

00:57:09.310 --> 00:57:12.250
It's incredible that you should have been married four times in five years.

00:57:14.490 --> 00:57:15.670
Why did you divorce Kavanaugh?

00:57:16.810 --> 00:57:19.690
Oh, Kavanaugh. Oh, he became a bore.

00:57:20.480 --> 00:57:21.340
The Baron de Brissac?

00:57:21.660 --> 00:57:22.700
He became a bore, too.

00:57:24.600 --> 00:57:25.840
And, and, uh, Lauderdale?

00:57:26.020 --> 00:57:27.800
Oh, he was the most awful bore of a lot.

00:57:28.390 --> 00:57:29.710
I'd much rather be married to a group.

00:57:31.820 --> 00:57:32.920
I hope I've not become a baller yet.

00:57:33.200 --> 00:57:35.180
Oh, no. I find you very interesting.

00:57:35.890 --> 00:57:36.970
Very, very amusing.

00:58:31.340 --> 00:58:47.870
What are you? Do you love me?

00:58:50.900 --> 00:58:59.110
It's not enough.

00:59:01.370 --> 00:59:02.570
I might be interested in you.

00:59:03.400 --> 00:59:04.300
That's still not enough.

00:59:07.220 --> 00:59:07.960
Please be frank with me.

00:59:10.230 --> 00:59:12.830
I thought that the greatest virtue of the modern woman was that absolute frank.

00:59:14.530 --> 00:59:15.370
I've been frank with you.

00:59:16.300 --> 00:59:22.360
Haven't I told you all about Brissac and Kavanaugh and Lauderdale?

00:59:23.790 --> 00:59:24.390
What do you want?

00:59:54.030 --> 00:59:54.390
What about Miller?

00:59:55.020 --> 00:59:55.940
Yes, what about Miller?

00:59:59.560 --> 00:59:59.880
Oh, Miller!

01:00:00.670 --> 01:00:01.170
An episode.

01:00:02.270 --> 01:00:02.970
In the middle of the second?

01:00:04.060 --> 01:00:05.120
Another episode, I suppose.

01:00:06.560 --> 01:00:06.760
Of course.

01:00:08.500 --> 01:00:10.360
Four marriages in five years and two episodes.

01:00:12.480 --> 01:00:13.980
You don't seem to appreciate my frankness.

01:00:14.330 --> 01:00:15.090
I think I'll go home.

01:00:15.970 --> 01:00:16.550
Oh, no, please.

01:00:16.710 --> 01:00:18.390
Really, I do appreciate your frankness.

01:00:18.710 --> 01:00:20.810
And I care so much that I can understand how it happened.

01:00:22.690 --> 01:00:27.960
You were poor before your first marriage.

01:00:28.240 --> 01:00:29.940
He offered you everything that made life worth living.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:32.320
How are you to know that the one essential thing was missing?

01:00:32.890 --> 01:00:33.450
How should you?

01:00:34.240 --> 01:00:35.260
Of course, the marriage failed.

01:00:35.820 --> 01:00:38.700
But a woman like you, a woman with ideals is just like a man.

01:00:38.780 --> 01:00:40.920
She has to go on searching until she finds the right man.

01:00:41.310 --> 01:00:41.990
The real man.

01:00:42.310 --> 01:00:43.730
The one man in the world for her.

01:00:44.980 --> 01:00:45.260
You?

01:00:45.480 --> 01:00:46.490
I hope so.

01:00:48.090 --> 01:00:50.140
Not of it, aren't you?

01:00:50.260 --> 01:00:54.740
You can never be sure of anything but the past like mine.

01:00:55.070 --> 01:00:57.960
Oh, but my darling, when a woman is in love, she has no power.

01:00:58.560 --> 01:00:59.180
She's reborn.

01:00:59.380 --> 01:00:59.980
She's an innocent...

01:01:01.430 --> 01:01:03.150
Don't you see, my darling, it's perfectly simple.

01:01:03.290 --> 01:01:04.330
That if only you could...

01:01:09.670 --> 01:01:11.180
Your husband, don't look.

01:01:12.070 --> 01:01:12.230
Where?

01:01:12.900 --> 01:01:13.480
Over there in the corner.

01:01:20.090 --> 01:01:21.770
If not, I just don't want a public brawl, that's all.

01:01:22.150 --> 01:01:23.170
Very well, let's go.

01:01:27.580 --> 01:01:29.980
The usual magnum for what?

01:01:35.820 --> 01:01:40.080
I'll take you home.

01:01:40.200 --> 01:01:41.360
No, no, that wouldn't do, thank you.

01:01:41.520 --> 01:01:42.060
I'll go home alone.

01:01:42.280 --> 01:01:42.520
Good night.

01:01:43.100 --> 01:01:43.880
Grosvenor Square, please.

01:01:44.300 --> 01:01:45.920
Yes, but what number, Grosvenor Square?

01:01:46.510 --> 01:01:47.050
Not telling.

01:01:48.600 --> 01:01:49.640
When shall I see you?

01:02:08.540 --> 01:02:09.240
Hello, Grandpa.

01:02:09.560 --> 01:02:11.350
Hello, Emily.

01:02:11.620 --> 01:02:12.500
Not at all.

01:02:13.010 --> 01:02:14.330
Proposals take some time.

01:02:14.610 --> 01:02:15.230
How did you know?

01:02:15.450 --> 01:02:20.430
Little girls having a special glitter in their eyes after a proposal, even today.

01:02:21.030 --> 01:02:22.730
You're a wise old man.

01:02:24.850 --> 01:02:27.030
Did you tell that jackass the truth about yourself?

01:02:27.550 --> 01:02:29.130
No, and he's not a jackass.

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:30.800
You think you're a cheap woman?

01:02:31.460 --> 01:02:32.560
He's a jackass.

01:02:33.020 --> 01:02:35.520
He thinks I'm the wickedest woman in the whole world.

01:02:35.970 --> 01:02:37.970
He thinks I've had four husbands and several...

01:02:37.970 --> 01:02:40.910
Did you tell him that you had four husbands and several...

01:02:40.910 --> 01:02:41.210
No.

01:02:41.970 --> 01:02:42.830
He told me.

01:02:43.090 --> 01:02:44.030
You know Lady Mere?

01:02:44.190 --> 01:02:44.450
Mm-hmm.

01:02:44.850 --> 01:02:46.730
Well, she was at the ball of the Royal Park Hotel,

01:02:46.970 --> 01:02:50.240
and she had a Winterhalter costume, too, and some adventurer.

01:02:52.120 --> 01:02:54.760
And Lord Mere's divorcing her, and Logan thinks I'm she.

01:02:56.320 --> 01:02:58.180
Thinks that you're Lady Mere?

01:02:58.670 --> 01:02:59.980
Yes, but he's very...

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:01.760
Very sympathetic and very understanding.

01:03:02.420 --> 01:03:07.400
He sees very clearly that my unfortunate past was one long search for the right man.

01:03:08.250 --> 01:03:08.750
Himself?

01:03:09.270 --> 01:03:14.380
Yes. And he also says that a woman is chased and reborn again when she's in love.

01:03:16.800 --> 01:03:21.150
I don't like the sound of that. He may get a shock when he discovers the truth.

01:03:22.240 --> 01:03:24.700
But aren't you a little cynical, Grandpa?

01:03:25.480 --> 01:03:29.210
I don't think so. And every day I learn things about...

01:03:30.030 --> 01:03:34.010
which even the cleverest grandchildren know nothing at all.

01:03:34.730 --> 01:03:37.960
But you don't mean that he might prefer a bad woman to, um...

01:03:37.960 --> 01:03:40.800
Very often. And so do you.

01:03:41.820 --> 01:03:45.660
Certainly. What made you play the woman with the past?

01:03:46.120 --> 01:03:49.560
Because you felt you could wear your imaginary adventures

01:03:49.560 --> 01:03:51.940
like an alluring costume, didn't you?

01:03:53.660 --> 01:03:55.680
Yes, and apparently with great success.

01:03:56.170 --> 01:03:59.260
The danger is that when the costume falls off...

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:03.280
The young man may look at you and wonder what on earth he saw

01:04:03.280 --> 01:04:06.780
in such an innocent little slip of a girl.

01:04:08.580 --> 01:04:12.100
Grandad, what shall I do? I love the brute so much.

01:04:20.080 --> 01:04:22.200
Paul Fryer's telephone to ask whether you really agree

01:04:22.200 --> 01:04:23.880
that the mere case brief should be prepared

01:04:23.880 --> 01:04:25.780
on the basis of the correspondent is unknown.

01:04:26.100 --> 01:04:26.560
I agree.

01:04:27.260 --> 01:04:29.240
But you know perfectly well that he's not unknown.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:33.280
It'll be disastrous for you if it comes out in court, who the co-respondent really is.

01:04:33.440 --> 01:04:33.780
I don't care.

01:04:39.610 --> 01:04:42.050
I'll get Lady Merehead her vote if I have to close up this shop.

01:04:47.620 --> 01:04:48.300
There you are.

01:04:48.750 --> 01:04:49.770
How are you, old boy?

01:04:50.050 --> 01:04:51.290
I hope you're terribly well.

01:04:51.470 --> 01:04:51.790
Thank you.

01:04:51.930 --> 01:04:52.930
Yes, I am terribly well.

01:04:53.030 --> 01:04:53.830
Yes, so am I.

01:04:54.160 --> 01:04:54.760
Terribly well?

01:04:54.960 --> 01:04:55.300
Yes.

01:04:55.860 --> 01:04:56.480
Terribly well.

01:04:57.360 --> 01:04:57.980
Well, what's happened?

01:04:58.480 --> 01:04:59.000
Admit her.

01:05:01.080 --> 01:05:07.720
My wife, she's superb, and Saunders, he's an idiot, and I'm a fool.

01:05:07.900 --> 01:05:11.280
The man in her room at the Royal Parks Hotel was the manager of the hotel.

01:05:11.440 --> 01:05:13.400
You were the only one that was right. You gave it to me at first.

01:05:13.660 --> 01:05:17.580
I owe my happiness entirely. She owes her happiness entirely to you.

01:05:18.140 --> 01:05:21.370
It's a new honeymoon for us. Thank you, old boy.

01:05:22.520 --> 01:05:25.130
By the way, I'm sorry to have troubled you in vain.

01:05:25.250 --> 01:05:25.390
Oh?

01:05:25.940 --> 01:05:27.260
Yes, yes, but I know how it is.

01:05:27.340 --> 01:05:29.980
But I said to my dear wife, I said, that fellow Logan's the most...

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:31.720
the most awfully decent chap in the world.

01:05:32.130 --> 01:05:33.390
At first, he refused our case.

01:05:33.430 --> 01:05:35.930
He refused a fat case sooner than to spoil our happiness.

01:05:36.580 --> 01:05:36.860
Goodbye.

01:05:37.570 --> 01:05:38.630
And what did she say?

01:05:39.210 --> 01:05:42.010
She said you were the most awfully decent fellow in the world.

01:05:42.320 --> 01:05:43.380
And so you are.

01:05:43.580 --> 01:05:49.970
A message?

01:05:50.340 --> 01:05:50.440
Yes.

01:05:51.540 --> 01:05:54.760
Do tell her from me that I think she's the most awfully clever woman in the world.

01:06:33.480 --> 01:06:34.060
Oh

01:07:08.090 --> 01:07:10.170
I can't open the door with your umbrella. Where's your key?

01:07:10.410 --> 01:07:12.070
Why do you have to come and open the door?

01:07:12.450 --> 01:07:13.110
Where's the butler?

01:07:13.350 --> 01:07:13.910
He's gone.

01:07:14.420 --> 01:07:14.780
Saunders?

01:07:15.070 --> 01:07:15.890
She's gone, too.

01:07:16.150 --> 01:07:16.670
And Coke?

01:07:17.780 --> 01:07:20.280
I fired them all. I won't have paid enemies in my own house.

01:07:22.940 --> 01:07:23.300
Pardon.

01:07:31.820 --> 01:07:37.350
It was the manager.

01:07:38.440 --> 01:07:39.780
What? Where? When?

01:07:40.040 --> 01:07:42.600
In your room at the Royal Parks Hotel. It was the hotel manager.

01:07:42.760 --> 01:07:43.140
It was not.

01:07:43.380 --> 01:07:44.920
You say it was not, then who was it?

01:07:45.080 --> 01:07:51.220
Oh, it was John, George, Ingleby, Thomas, a president, a prime minister, and a baritone.

01:07:51.320 --> 01:07:52.660
You're just trying to confuse me.

01:07:53.180 --> 01:07:54.220
What do you want? A divorce?

01:07:54.440 --> 01:07:57.100
All right. You can have it. Get out of here.

01:07:57.320 --> 01:07:59.010
Get out of here. Go and see your lawyer.

01:07:59.090 --> 01:07:59.290
See them.

01:08:32.460 --> 01:08:39.950
Your wife is the most awfully clever woman in the world.

01:08:53.340 --> 01:08:57.780
What do you mean my wife is the most awfully clever woman in the world?

01:09:02.560 --> 01:09:07.340
Ah, good.

01:09:07.700 --> 01:09:08.380
How much is that?

01:09:08.620 --> 01:09:09.780
Eight and nine cents, my lord.

01:09:10.000 --> 01:09:11.700
What, eight and nine cents for whiskey and soda?

01:09:11.920 --> 01:09:12.940
That's five you've had, sir.

01:09:13.020 --> 01:09:14.220
Four doubles already in this one.

01:09:14.420 --> 01:09:14.620
Good.

01:09:15.920 --> 01:09:17.270
Thank you, my lord.

01:09:20.640 --> 01:09:22.040
What's your opinion of women, Peter?

01:09:22.660 --> 01:09:24.720
Well, my lord, they have their uses, as we know.

01:09:24.880 --> 01:09:26.780
But as for consorting with them, as you might say,

01:09:27.000 --> 01:09:28.020
I've only dabbled in it.

01:09:28.080 --> 01:09:29.160
Well, you leave it at that.

01:09:29.240 --> 01:09:29.980
Women in a minute.

01:09:32.720 --> 01:09:34.110
What? The Foreign Secretary, sir?

01:09:34.330 --> 01:09:37.180
Oh, you fool. The Garden of Eden, Adam and Eve.

01:09:37.790 --> 01:09:38.490
You know the story?

01:09:39.080 --> 01:09:41.000
Yes, I've heard of it, sir. It was a bit before my time.

01:09:41.060 --> 01:09:42.180
Yes, but it's still going on.

01:09:42.750 --> 01:09:44.690
The woman leads the man up the garden path

01:09:44.690 --> 01:09:49.300
and leaves him in the lurch, naked in the grass at the Royal Park Hotel.

01:09:49.560 --> 01:09:51.760
Oh, can't say I ever heard that bit, sir.

01:09:52.400 --> 01:09:55.210
True. I can't do that sort of thing to me.

01:09:56.420 --> 01:09:58.600
I'm the last man to hang about where I'm not wanted.

01:09:59.210 --> 01:09:59.870
You know that, Peter.

01:10:00.060 --> 01:10:00.760
Yes, sir, Lord.

01:10:01.160 --> 01:10:01.960
Good night, dear.

01:10:02.140 --> 01:10:02.720
Good night, sir.

01:10:04.210 --> 01:10:05.190
Test these cigars.

01:10:09.080 --> 01:10:09.440
Pickle.

01:10:30.060 --> 01:10:30.520
Thank you.

01:11:04.990 --> 01:11:08.060
Hello? Yes, Mrs. Logan.

01:11:08.530 --> 01:11:12.330
Must see you, old boy. Must see you, old boy.

01:11:13.130 --> 01:11:14.570
Matter of life and death.

01:11:15.260 --> 01:11:18.070
What? What? Three o'clock!

01:11:18.860 --> 01:11:22.120
I know, but I'm right around to see you.

01:11:22.400 --> 01:11:23.640
Matter of life and death.

01:11:32.720 --> 01:11:46.200
Why did you say my wife was the most wonderfully clever woman in the world?

01:11:47.100 --> 01:11:48.780
No, look here, it's three o'clock.

01:11:48.780 --> 01:11:53.180
Why did you say my wife was the most wonderfully clever woman in the world?

01:11:53.570 --> 01:11:55.570
Sometimes one just says things for something to say.

01:11:55.730 --> 01:11:59.970
No, loyal chaps make your masses of money because...

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:01.920
You don't say things just for something to say.

01:12:02.340 --> 01:12:07.550
Why? Why did you say my wife was the most wonderfully clever woman of the world?

01:12:08.580 --> 01:12:16.080
Sit down. I thought your wife was very clever.

01:12:17.740 --> 01:12:19.860
To make it up with you after the royal party.

01:12:20.300 --> 01:12:23.940
Mmm. She's very clever. You're very clever.

01:12:24.980 --> 01:12:26.160
But I'm very clever, too.

01:12:27.710 --> 01:12:28.530
I wish I weren't.

01:12:28.780 --> 01:12:29.120
Mind what?

01:12:29.420 --> 01:12:29.800
Clevers.

01:12:30.060 --> 01:12:31.770
Subtle, clear-sighted.

01:12:33.260 --> 01:12:34.480
I should be a happier man.

01:12:34.580 --> 01:12:35.100
What's the trouble?

01:12:35.820 --> 01:12:37.020
He doesn't love me any more.

01:12:37.700 --> 01:12:38.200
What do you mean?

01:12:38.340 --> 01:12:40.280
I thought you said that you'd made it up with her.

01:12:40.610 --> 01:12:42.600
Yes, I've got a sixth sense.

01:12:43.380 --> 01:12:45.240
Subtlety, knowledge of women.

01:12:46.400 --> 01:12:48.960
She loves the man from the Royal Park Hotel.

01:13:03.640 --> 01:13:05.020
I've got something very important to tell you.

01:13:13.960 --> 01:13:16.040
I am the man from the Royal Parks Hotel.

01:13:17.480 --> 01:13:19.080
You as you can't be. You're a barrister.

01:13:20.760 --> 01:13:22.860
Your wife spent the night in one of my rooms.

01:13:23.470 --> 01:13:26.650
Don't dare to suspect her. Nothing happened.

01:13:27.440 --> 01:13:28.580
And why are you telling me this?

01:13:29.070 --> 01:13:29.730
Because I love her.

01:13:30.860 --> 01:13:34.010
And if you're going to divorce her, then I'm going to marry her.

01:13:34.490 --> 01:13:39.290
If she's going to marry you, if she's in love with you...

01:13:47.220 --> 01:13:49.370
Don't limit it, chump, sky high.

01:13:49.890 --> 01:13:50.130
Who?

01:13:50.720 --> 01:13:51.730
Clement. Who's Clement?

01:13:52.250 --> 01:13:54.090
Found the rotter filthy with money.

01:13:54.170 --> 01:13:55.010
Well, what's he got to do with her?

01:13:55.400 --> 01:13:56.120
He's in love with her.

01:13:56.160 --> 01:13:56.940
But is she in love with him?

01:13:57.120 --> 01:13:57.780
Certainly not.

01:13:58.560 --> 01:13:59.980
If she's in love with you, how can she be...

01:14:00.600 --> 01:14:01.920
She's not that sort of woman.

01:14:04.140 --> 01:14:09.680
Sit down, have a drink.

01:14:12.920 --> 01:14:16.680
If I've got to divorce her, I prefer you as a limit.

01:14:17.480 --> 01:14:17.860
You're a gentleman.

01:14:18.580 --> 01:14:19.480
Limit is not.

01:14:20.040 --> 01:14:20.880
Limit is not.

01:14:21.520 --> 01:14:22.140
Limit isn't.

01:14:23.760 --> 01:14:24.620
Tell her, and I'll tell her.

01:14:24.720 --> 01:14:25.420
Don't you worry.

01:14:26.510 --> 01:14:27.070
I'll tell her.

01:14:28.880 --> 01:14:29.680
Logan's a gentleman.

01:14:30.570 --> 01:14:31.090
Limits.

01:14:53.370 --> 01:14:53.930
Who are you?

01:14:55.650 --> 01:14:58.480
I belong to the law.

01:15:11.580 --> 01:15:13.430
Darling, I'm wise and gentle.

01:15:14.820 --> 01:15:15.240
You're drunk.

01:15:15.540 --> 01:15:18.090
I'm not, and you'll see it, because I've come to tell you this.

01:15:18.780 --> 01:15:19.540
Logan's a gentleman.

01:15:20.670 --> 01:15:21.170
Then it is.

01:15:23.050 --> 01:15:23.970
Who is Logan?

01:15:24.170 --> 01:15:24.830
Lawyer chapter.

01:15:25.960 --> 01:15:28.410
You take him, he'll break my heart.

01:15:29.390 --> 01:15:29.750
I wish you.

01:15:31.210 --> 01:15:32.490
Why should I take him?

01:15:32.760 --> 01:15:33.680
In love with him.

01:15:33.820 --> 01:15:35.460
In love with him.

01:15:35.950 --> 01:15:36.770
Who told you that?

01:15:37.010 --> 01:15:37.750
Logan himself.

01:15:39.070 --> 01:15:41.920
He said, break my heart.

01:15:46.550 --> 01:15:47.590
Oh, I see.

01:15:48.650 --> 01:15:49.930
So you're willing to divorce me

01:15:49.930 --> 01:15:52.610
so somebody by the name of Logan can marry me.

01:15:53.000 --> 01:15:53.580
Is that it?

01:15:53.980 --> 01:15:56.230
Break my heart that I wish you a heaven.

01:15:56.490 --> 01:15:58.000
Will you please get out of here?

01:15:58.080 --> 01:15:59.180
Go to your club and go to bed.

01:16:02.040 --> 01:16:02.580
I wish you.

01:16:18.530 --> 01:16:19.030
Thank you.

01:16:32.680 --> 01:16:33.240
Molyneux?

01:16:34.390 --> 01:16:34.710
Pecker?

01:16:37.680 --> 01:16:38.660
Who do you wish to say?

01:16:41.470 --> 01:16:41.790
Please.

01:16:42.390 --> 01:16:43.410
Well, what names, please?

01:16:44.210 --> 01:16:44.790
Lady Mare.

01:16:46.620 --> 01:16:47.680
Did you say Lady Mare?

01:16:48.750 --> 01:16:49.450
Are you Lady Mare?

01:16:51.080 --> 01:16:51.740
But who are you?

01:16:54.260 --> 01:16:55.320
Oh, Lady Mare, come with me, please.

01:17:01.440 --> 01:17:01.860
What's the matter?

01:17:02.040 --> 01:17:03.680
Come away from here and I'll tell you all about it.

01:17:04.030 --> 01:17:04.710
Well, who are you?

01:17:05.170 --> 01:17:06.070
Where have you went from here?

01:17:06.190 --> 01:17:06.950
The hairdressers.

01:17:07.050 --> 01:17:07.390
Who are they?

01:17:07.850 --> 01:17:08.130
Chevaliers.

01:17:09.020 --> 01:17:09.280
Come along.

01:17:13.930 --> 01:17:14.230
Where is she?

01:17:14.330 --> 01:17:16.480
Well, they were here, sir.

01:17:17.620 --> 01:17:18.060
What do you mean they?

01:17:18.180 --> 01:17:18.580
Where is she?

01:17:19.010 --> 01:17:19.810
She was too, sir.

01:17:23.160 --> 01:17:26.170
No, you opened the door and she came in.

01:17:26.400 --> 01:17:27.240
They came in, sir.

01:17:29.520 --> 01:17:29.780
What?

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:30.700
What did you ask?

01:17:30.990 --> 01:17:31.810
What name, madam?

01:17:33.050 --> 01:17:34.110
And what did she say?

01:17:34.430 --> 01:17:35.490
They said Lady Mere.

01:17:36.120 --> 01:17:36.320
She?

01:17:36.820 --> 01:17:37.120
They?

01:17:38.340 --> 01:17:39.820
One lady said Lady Mere.

01:17:39.960 --> 01:17:40.340
Two, sir.

01:17:42.020 --> 01:17:42.640
Were two ladies here?

01:17:42.800 --> 01:17:43.200
Two, sir.

01:17:43.380 --> 01:17:44.460
And two ladies said Lady Mere.

01:17:44.580 --> 01:17:44.980
Two, sir.

01:17:46.040 --> 01:17:46.600
Where are they then?

01:17:48.600 --> 01:17:49.760
Well, they just disappeared, sir.

01:17:50.790 --> 01:17:51.730
You better disappear too.

01:17:52.310 --> 01:17:54.710
Go back to your father and tell him I've no use for a congenital idiot.

01:17:57.390 --> 01:17:58.590
Could have sworn there were two.

01:18:01.310 --> 01:18:04.290
So I went off to the divorce court to see Mr. Logan do his stuff.

01:18:04.620 --> 01:18:05.760
They tell me he's very clever.

01:18:06.220 --> 01:18:06.580
Clever.

01:18:07.210 --> 01:18:10.470
If you call clever bullying and brow-beating somebody who can't hit back.

01:18:11.220 --> 01:18:12.680
And he knows nothing at all about women.

01:18:12.860 --> 01:18:13.640
Do any of them?

01:18:14.350 --> 01:18:17.090
There was some wretched creature in the box called Mrs. Johnson or something,

01:18:17.190 --> 01:18:18.570
and Logan was acting for her husband.

01:18:18.940 --> 01:18:20.280
And what do you think he said about women?

01:18:20.860 --> 01:18:21.620
Could have been anything.

01:18:22.270 --> 01:18:25.230
He said we were merciless, stupid, brainless, and hopeless.

01:18:25.660 --> 01:18:26.760
But you know, he's not far wrong.

01:18:27.220 --> 01:18:27.780
Anything else?

01:18:28.240 --> 01:18:29.900
Yes, he said we'd be spent half our time.

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:31.880
wondering which part of our bodies to faint next.

01:18:32.900 --> 01:18:35.750
Oh, well, my dear, now, that is a lie.

01:18:44.340 --> 01:18:45.020
What do you think of it?

01:18:45.220 --> 01:18:46.120
I think it's swell.

01:18:46.860 --> 01:18:48.500
I wonder if Mr. Logan would approve.

01:18:48.840 --> 01:18:50.940
If you ask me, I think that guy needs a lesson.

01:18:51.140 --> 01:18:52.880
He certainly does, and I'm going to give it to him.

01:18:53.360 --> 01:18:55.700
He's in a blue funk about that night at the Royal Fox Hotel.

01:18:56.160 --> 01:18:58.640
He thinks he's going to be cited as Lady Mayor's correspondent.

01:19:00.830 --> 01:19:01.890
See, that's very funny.

01:19:02.070 --> 01:19:03.690
I can hardly wait till we get home

01:19:03.690 --> 01:19:05.170
and tell a little worry boy about this.

01:19:05.270 --> 01:19:06.590
You know, he'll swallow his gamp teeth

01:19:06.590 --> 01:19:07.310
and everything else.

01:19:08.090 --> 01:19:09.530
Good night.

01:19:11.930 --> 01:19:12.770
Show number to telephone.

01:19:13.410 --> 01:19:14.970
Quite sure no lady telephone.

01:19:15.780 --> 01:19:16.160
Good night.

01:19:39.720 --> 01:19:40.100
Good night, sir.

01:19:46.440 --> 01:19:48.390
Lady Muir wants to speak to Mr. Logan.

01:19:49.250 --> 01:19:52.040
Hold on. Mr. Logan, sir.

01:19:52.480 --> 01:19:53.000
Lady Muir.

01:19:53.220 --> 01:19:53.380
Where?

01:19:53.780 --> 01:19:54.260
On the telephone.

01:19:56.680 --> 01:19:58.000
Ask her, sir, if she was two.

01:19:58.160 --> 01:19:58.360
Goodnight.

01:20:04.510 --> 01:20:04.750
Hello?

01:20:05.440 --> 01:20:07.360
Oh, is that you?

01:20:11.880 --> 01:20:12.300
Why didn't you?

01:20:13.350 --> 01:20:14.510
Because I don't like your office.

01:20:16.140 --> 01:20:16.920
Where can I see you?

01:20:17.940 --> 01:20:18.300
Where?

01:20:18.540 --> 01:20:19.440
Well, let me see.

01:20:20.700 --> 01:20:22.600
Why don't you come to Mayor Hall for the weekend?

01:20:24.250 --> 01:20:26.130
Mayor Hall, in Hampshire, you know it.

01:20:27.260 --> 01:20:29.710
Yes, I know, but do you think that would be right?

01:20:32.170 --> 01:20:33.550
No, wait, wait, wait.

01:20:33.730 --> 01:20:36.250
But if you don't want to see me.

01:20:36.760 --> 01:20:40.930
Well, of course I want to see you, but has Lord Mere not told you?

01:20:42.300 --> 01:20:43.640
Lord Mere has told me everything.

01:20:44.530 --> 01:20:47.320
And do you think that his place would be the right place?

01:20:47.840 --> 01:20:50.460
The only place, but of course if you don't want to come.

01:20:50.830 --> 01:20:52.370
But of course I want to see you. When?

01:20:53.860 --> 01:20:54.220
Saturday.

01:20:55.110 --> 01:20:57.250
Right, Saturday evening.

01:20:57.880 --> 01:20:58.700
All right, good night.

01:21:48.620 --> 01:21:50.380
Yes, I think so, if they're not too big.

01:21:50.520 --> 01:21:51.600
Nothing's too big for that, Mayor.

01:21:51.720 --> 01:21:53.360
If you want a pilot, keep your eye on my wife.

01:21:53.890 --> 01:21:54.450
She's good, is she?

01:21:54.550 --> 01:21:56.530
This hand I ever saw, heart like a lion.

01:21:58.660 --> 01:21:59.520
And she's talking to.

01:22:02.170 --> 01:22:04.340
Why Ed, it's that cad limit.

01:22:05.210 --> 01:22:06.050
Why cad?

01:22:06.390 --> 01:22:07.030
Awful fella.

01:22:07.660 --> 01:22:10.360
Shoots foxes all the summer, rides over hounds half the winter.

01:22:11.460 --> 01:22:13.140
And what does he do with his spare time?

01:22:13.440 --> 01:22:14.860
Makes up to other fella's wives.

01:22:15.080 --> 01:22:16.920
But if he thinks he's got a chance with Claire,

01:22:17.140 --> 01:22:18.480
he's barking up the wrong tree.

01:22:20.570 --> 01:22:22.510
I'll meet you at the Barclay at 3 on Thursday.

01:22:23.400 --> 01:22:25.260
By the way, what time are you expecting your friend Logan?

01:22:26.160 --> 01:22:27.740
Oh, I should think around tea time.

01:22:27.920 --> 01:22:28.600
He's driving down.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:30.500
Right?

01:23:06.430 --> 01:23:07.090
He's coming to see you.

01:23:07.580 --> 01:23:08.310
Hello, sir.

01:23:08.450 --> 01:23:09.030
I'm glad to see you.

01:23:09.270 --> 01:23:09.890
Come on, my dear.

01:23:10.010 --> 01:23:10.930
She's showing us all the way.

01:23:12.570 --> 01:23:16.110
I see you two haven't made it up again, have you?

01:23:16.680 --> 01:23:17.960
I don't know what you mean by made it up,

01:23:18.000 --> 01:23:19.480
but he's been very sweet to me.

01:23:19.600 --> 01:23:20.320
Oh, well, that's up with it.

01:23:20.460 --> 01:23:21.040
That is why.

01:23:21.160 --> 01:23:21.680
Well, I'm not coming.

01:23:22.180 --> 01:23:23.080
You must. You've accepted.

01:23:23.260 --> 01:23:23.840
I can't help it.

01:23:24.080 --> 01:23:25.640
In the fellow's house, it's all wrong.

01:23:26.800 --> 01:23:28.120
Very well then, if you don't want to see me.

01:23:28.340 --> 01:23:29.460
No, I do, but look here.

01:23:29.580 --> 01:23:29.960
Are you...

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:31.020
Are you going to marry me, are you not?

01:23:31.060 --> 01:23:31.780
I'll tell you tonight.

01:23:31.960 --> 01:23:32.860
Yes, but look here.

01:23:32.980 --> 01:23:33.180
Tonight!

01:23:34.500 --> 01:23:50.020
I'm sure Mr. Logan would come down.

01:23:50.200 --> 01:23:51.800
The suspense is killing me.

01:23:52.040 --> 01:23:52.440
Me too.

01:23:52.580 --> 01:23:54.860
I bet he feels an awful ass when he finds out who's which.

01:23:55.060 --> 01:23:55.120
What?

01:23:56.080 --> 01:23:57.920
Then don't make it worse by laughing at him.

01:23:58.120 --> 01:23:58.760
Seat this here.

01:24:00.540 --> 01:24:06.330
Oh, and Clare, you sit there, will you, please?

01:24:06.550 --> 01:24:06.830
Mm-hmm.

01:24:07.550 --> 01:24:10.710
And Grandpa, oh, Grandpa, you'll find where you are.

01:24:11.430 --> 01:24:13.390
Oh, and Clare, when he comes in, will you please say,

01:24:13.490 --> 01:24:15.030
you know Miss Leslie's team?

01:24:15.380 --> 01:24:15.700
Mm-hmm.

01:24:16.560 --> 01:24:19.260
And I'll stand here now.

01:24:21.380 --> 01:24:21.500
Good.

01:24:30.410 --> 01:24:31.210
Mr. Logan.

01:24:35.750 --> 01:24:39.260
Mr. Logan, it's nice of you to come down at such short notice.

01:24:39.710 --> 01:24:40.810
Do you know Lord Steele?

01:24:41.030 --> 01:24:41.750
Yes, of course I do.

01:24:41.870 --> 01:24:44.000
And, of course, you know Horan.

01:24:44.840 --> 01:24:45.100
Yes.

01:24:46.250 --> 01:24:59.830
And this is Miss Steele, Miss Leslie.

01:25:00.460 --> 01:25:22.720
I don't know Miss Thiel, and I don't want to know Miss Thiel.

01:25:24.010 --> 01:25:26.970
I think that Miss Thiel is a very unpleasant, dishonest young woman.

01:25:27.490 --> 01:25:29.330
I say, old boy, don't lose a sense of humor.

01:25:29.510 --> 01:25:29.970
It's only a bit of f...

01:25:30.090 --> 01:25:31.450
Well, you go on having your bit of fun.

01:25:32.710 --> 01:25:35.590
You have your bit of fun with Lemmett, and you have your bit of fun with the hotel manager.

01:25:36.690 --> 01:25:39.650
Miss Steele can have her bit of fun with the next poor fool that falls in love with her.

01:25:40.740 --> 01:25:42.260
In fact, you're a damn funny lot, couldn't I?

01:25:43.260 --> 01:25:45.520
Well, what do you think of that?

01:25:45.780 --> 01:25:46.620
Why, Jo, what?

01:25:46.970 --> 01:25:47.190
Huh?

01:25:49.460 --> 01:25:51.270
Grandpa, did you hear what he said?

01:25:51.490 --> 01:25:52.290
Yes, darling.

01:25:52.650 --> 01:25:53.810
Good, wasn't it?

01:26:20.220 --> 01:26:22.540
50 years ago, I didn't understand.

01:26:22.880 --> 01:26:29.960
I think he's right. You're not...

01:26:30.000 --> 01:26:31.200
You're not going to let him get away with it, are you?

01:26:31.680 --> 01:26:34.370
No, I'm not. Up to now, he's been after me.

01:26:34.800 --> 01:26:35.780
Now I'm going after him.

01:26:36.790 --> 01:26:43.160
He left no address.

01:26:43.420 --> 01:26:43.680
None.

01:26:44.650 --> 01:26:45.910
Didn't he say when he was coming back?

01:26:46.090 --> 01:26:46.910
Yes, never.

01:26:47.620 --> 01:26:48.500
What about his work?

01:26:48.660 --> 01:26:49.040
Chuck did.

01:26:49.460 --> 01:26:51.660
And he had the case of a lifetime coming on next week.

01:26:51.820 --> 01:26:52.180
What's that?

01:26:52.320 --> 01:26:53.440
The Strangeway's divorce.

01:26:54.110 --> 01:26:55.210
Four correspondence.

01:26:55.620 --> 01:26:56.640
Been the making of him.

01:26:57.170 --> 01:26:58.270
But isn't there anything to be done?

01:26:58.850 --> 01:26:59.890
Not unless you stop the trade.

01:27:00.000 --> 01:27:00.560
Train?

01:27:01.850 --> 01:27:02.870
The boat train at Victoria.

01:27:03.130 --> 01:27:03.450
What time?

01:27:03.570 --> 01:27:04.250
11 o'clock.

01:27:06.280 --> 01:27:06.920
Here, hey, whoa!

01:28:01.530 --> 01:28:09.460
Come on, darling. Better now.

01:28:09.720 --> 01:28:09.840
Mm.

01:28:10.920 --> 01:28:12.060
Nasty pain all gone.

01:28:12.300 --> 01:28:12.380
Mm.

01:28:18.020 --> 01:28:19.240
You've chosen the sweetest house.

01:28:22.580 --> 01:28:23.480
Pretty sure of me, aren't you?

01:28:24.410 --> 01:28:26.410
Well, you were so desperately in love with me.

01:28:26.590 --> 01:28:27.510
Do I have any say in the matter?

01:28:28.140 --> 01:28:29.970
Yes. You can ask me to marry you.

01:28:31.900 --> 01:28:33.780
Well, will you?

01:28:35.070 --> 01:28:35.510
I might.

01:28:39.730 --> 01:28:39.930
Why?

01:28:41.560 --> 01:28:42.800
We'll be married in Paris at once.

01:28:43.670 --> 01:28:45.450
And we'll honeymoon on the Riviera for six weeks.

01:28:45.930 --> 01:28:46.210
No!

01:28:46.510 --> 01:28:47.850
Have you forgotten the strange ways case?

01:28:48.160 --> 01:28:49.000
Chance of a lifetime.

01:28:49.610 --> 01:28:50.330
Be the making of you.

01:28:50.430 --> 01:28:51.190
Four correspondence.

01:28:51.830 --> 01:28:53.810
We'll wire the office right away that we'll take the case.

01:28:54.480 --> 01:28:56.460
We'll wire the office right away that we're on our honeymoon.

01:28:56.540 --> 01:28:57.040
Oh, no.

01:28:57.280 --> 01:28:57.780
Oh, yes.

01:28:57.840 --> 01:28:58.260
Oh, no.

01:28:58.640 --> 01:28:59.400
Oh, yes.

01:29:01.080 --> 01:29:03.540
M'lord, there is one very simple explanation of this case.

01:29:04.570 --> 01:29:07.710
My client, Mrs. Strangeways, is a woman.

01:29:08.700 --> 01:29:10.960
That unique and perfect achievement of the human species

01:29:10.960 --> 01:29:13.540
is specially evolved for the comfort and solace of man.

01:29:14.600 --> 01:29:17.620
A tender, delicate organism put into this rough world

01:29:17.620 --> 01:29:20.850
to make life a little brighter and a little happier

01:29:20.850 --> 01:29:23.390
by her beauty and by her tenderness.

01:29:23.780 --> 01:29:26.860
And I say it advisedly, by her purity.

01:29:27.410 --> 01:29:29.970
M'lord, I admit that the allegation that she was found locked in the bar...

01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:33.260
from which two of the correspondents points to a certain lack of discretion on her part.

01:29:33.360 --> 01:29:36.420
But against that, my lord, we have her positive assurance that nothing happens.

01:29:37.990 --> 01:29:43.500
My lord, if we refuse to accept this statement, I submit that we strike a blow at the very foundation

01:29:43.500 --> 01:29:48.350
of the most sublime, the most idyllic, and the most delightful institution in the whole fabric

01:29:48.350 --> 01:29:59.980
of our civilization, the state of Mary. In my view, my lord, Mrs. Strangeways is guilty on one count.

01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:04.280
and upon one count alone, she is guilty of being a woman.

01:30:05.330 --> 01:30:07.390
Well, Lord, that is the explanation of Mrs. Logan.

01:30:07.490 --> 01:30:10.190
Mrs. Strangeway, and that is the explanation of this case.

01:30:10.430 --> 01:30:11.410
You may stand out.
